**SINGLE COMMAND LINE to find desired file within certain conditions**

find . -type f -size 1033c ! -executable -exec file {} \; | grep text


**What I learned:** 

-exec file {} \;

👉 “For each file you find, run the file command on it”

Very important part:

-exec → “do a command”

file → checks what kind of file it is

{} → “this file”

\; → “end of command”
